        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Piccalilli is a British pickled vegetable preserve with a sharp, mustardy sauce coloured vivid yellow by turmeric. The vegetables are "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "dry-brine",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dry-brine"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "d overnight first to keep them crisp, then covered in a cooked mustard-vinegar sauce. The resulting preserve is pungent when first made and mellows to something altogether more complex after 4 weeks in the jar. Makes about four 350 g jars."
          }
        ]
      },
